WEBVTT

00:10:28.236 --> 00:10:30.436
And this was an interesting
moment for the team

00:10:30.476 --> 00:10:32.396
because it's quite an emotional moment,

00:10:32.396 --> 00:10:34.996
because we'd spent and invested
so much time and energy

00:10:35.036 --> 00:10:36.636
into this ichthyosaur excavation

00:10:36.636 --> 00:10:38.996
that this moment captured that final piece

00:10:38.996 --> 00:10:41.596
where we're removing this
from its final resting place,

00:10:41.636 --> 00:10:43.556
180 million years ago.

00:10:48.036 --> 00:10:51.436
On January 10, 2022,

00:10:51.476 --> 00:10:57.156
this is almost one year after Joe
had made that incredible discovery,

00:10:57.196 --> 00:10:59.996
Angling Water and the University
of Manchester